  "reading_note": "The selected attribution backend is `lexical`, which has no parameter fitted on a calibration split -- it scores a span against the sentences of its own context and nothing else. Its top-1 accuracy therefore CANNOT degrade under a task shift, and a zero drop in that column is a property of the scorer rather than evidence of robustness. What genuinely transfers, or fails to, is the conformal quantile and the abstention threshold, and both are reported against their in-task counterparts."
